{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head d0354e266df022dbaf9730ab9e23039d60b340d5 (tree 07491457c6e00271a35d61fbf6474e47d9c74386). Assigned source review, all 172 filed artifacts, primary 39b0e3c79f0afd4369e507d106401a76c7671b0d first. Implementation binding is ONLY milestone request 53f838516a3b3f07689d60ee6c2495949575541e / producer promise ef3bc2501a6177a767f37f98ee1bd9a7092f987a. This is not full I3 or platform acceptance.\n\nFour P2 findings:\n\n1. Malformed runner report can leave a job durably started without an outcome. packages/checkers/src/outcome.ts:89–95 admits string environment fields, including a lone U+D800. judgment at :129 and provenance at :159 invoke configuration.ts:64 canonicalBytes, whose canonical string validation throws on that string. service.ts:262–265 computes judgment and provenance before keep, without handling that failure; the initial conclusion (:257) and recovery lookup (:217) leave this path outside the runner catch. A report with matching image, complete checkout and end, but that environment string passes the guard and throws before the signed durable check-error. Recovery encounters the same report; the one-run rule prevents starting again. Validate all canonicalized fields and provide safe malformed-report provenance so an invalid report produces a durable check-error. Owner should witness initial completion and recovery/resend with the same answer and no second run. Evidence: checker preliminary 03079a0809b4f6d316f1ce93403f1961a08b4320.\n\n2. Background outcome commits do not reliably publish to existing streams. packages/scope/src/object.ts:160–163 calls follow before starting the background dispatcher/operations; :172–175 publishes only that current head. operations.ts:339–342 can clear the final driver alarm when no walk or held work remains; :394 records a late answer and wakes without follow. The final outbox outcome removes its pending send (sqlite store nextSend excludes outcomes), leaving no guaranteed future alarm. An authorized stream waiting at h can remain there after the background outcome commits h+1, until an unrelated event rescues it. Publish after every successful background commit, including late answers, preserving authorization, disconnect, ordering and buffer rules. Owner should witness a pending stream receiving that final commit without a rescue write or alarm. This concerns the delivered runtime port; the default NO_OUTSIDE adapter is still unwired. Evidence: 2500230077ed876fa549e859b0eb41fe55fb0bcd2.\n\n3. Snapshot object deduplication is quadratic within the stated bounds. packages/git/src/snapshot.ts:213 scans the entire accumulated objects array with some for each distinct tree. A depth-two root with 19,999 directories, each containing the same verified blob under a distinct leaf name, has 20,000 distinct trees and 19,999 files within the documented bounds, but performs 199,990,000 tree-ID comparisons. This is a static operation count, not a timing or production denial-of-service claim. Keep an ID set alongside the ordered objects array, preserving postorder, IDs and output. Do not lower bounds or functionality to avoid the issue. Owner should witness output equivalence and bounded deduplication work. Evidence: 8c60a4ba205fa519ed24faaebdabc7c6ad7b55cf2.\n\n4. A retained snapshot is rejected by the object read route. packages/scope/src/reads.ts:162 permits definition, entry, rule and text only, so snapshot is rejected before the existing size-first stored-object check. operations.ts:414–433 and turn.ts:319 retain the named snapshot in the seal transaction, while packages/replay/src/source.ts:137 requests /snapshot/\u003cdigest\u003e through this route. An authorized reader therefore receives not-found even when the snapshot is stored. EL7 supplies the snapshot kind; EU2 requires reading it by digest before the ancestry walk. EX6 defers domain-keyed value reads, not snapshot reads. Admit snapshot while preserving authorization, size-first limits and missing/oversize refusal. Owner should witness an authenticated HTTP source reading an actual retained snapshot. Ancestry traversal remains explicitly owed; this fix must not claim replay consistency. Evidence: 5c3b6af6bd34a8d3cd8fc81399cee1b949c496602.\n\nCoverage and validation: fresh collective FULL reads covered all 172 current changed/added bodies (3,040,812 bytes; 41,956 LF), their complete native deltas (1,734,889 bytes), and all 42 removed paths' complete native U3 deletion delta (347,102 bytes; 6,900 LF). Root read all five reader reports and complete ledgers, the deletion report and complete ledger, all filed artifact statements, and focused finding contexts. Native bindings matched all 172 current blobs; all 344 body/delta intervals and the deletion intervals are gap-free; all 42 removed paths are absent at this head. Whole 214-path native U3 total is 2,081,991 bytes. This is collective coverage, not a claim that root personally read every source body. Root binding: /tmp/artroom-checker-m2-d035-ordinary-root-binding.json, 533829 bytes, SHA-256 5f8e5b4b9f2f67878455498d6ead5a8029f3a008312669446dac74cff07a12db.\n\nProducer-reported single gate: bf584e0c19c837c8d856fefaf75f1414063df90d, packages tree 434f4a7e5ad735dfcdec056a6264da21cc9bd2f1, unchanged at d035. Producer reports 497 Vitest tests in 67 files plus six Node tests and typecheck, 15.7 seconds elapsed on a warm shared Apple host. Post-gate change is the primary note only. Checker verified native custody and read docs/testing.md; checker did not run tests, gate or project diagnostics.\n\nArchitecture, security and simplification: current G30 old/new tree-link repair is credited at this exact head; trusted bounded-tree caller and declared review forms remain owed. Fail-closed authority/read adapters, explicit incomplete replay and explicit missing runtime owners are useful boundaries. Current runnable inbox/rules/membership do not make register, directory or destination founding runnable. Real runner/host/custody/storage, scopes deployment, immediate checker job read revocation, filtered snapshots, value reads, ancestry walk, extent callers/forms, all five capacity dimensions, browser identity/two-device recovery, I4/I5/IA/E1 and remaining source/UI joins remain owned work. Session residual-read policy is an adopted policy, not a new immediate-revocation defect. The authored-effects/derived-capacity distinction and undeclared review extent forms are already open work; no unsupported admission-history finding is promoted. The deleted parked source differences remain in functional scope.\n\nRepair these four defects with focused owner witnesses and the required single gate on the repair candidate. Estimates do not reduce scope. This review grants no landing, deployment, production-capacity, full-I3 or platform closure.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:39b0e3c79f0afd4369e507d106401a76c7671b0d","binding":"assigned","head":"d0354e266df022dbaf9730ab9e23039d60b340d5","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:50411e05d8055baec1627239d460928b9a510908\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ef3bc2501a6177a767f37f98ee1bd9a7092f987a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:170e8249ca94fad3bb4cb32c84b395791ae58a15","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}